* N-QUEENS DEMO (4x4)
* -------------------
* Solves the 4-queens puzzle by backtracking and prints both solutions.
* Place one queen per row; for row R the queen sits in column Q<R>.
* A placement is legal when no other queen shares its column or either
* diagonal. We track which columns/diagonals are occupied with three
* "used" arrays so each check is O(1):
*   UC<c>     column c is in use
*   D1<R+c>   the "/" diagonal R+c is in use      (indices 2..8)
*   D2<R-c+4> the "\" diagonal R-c is in use      (offset by 4 so it's >=1)
* Algorithm: at row R try Q<R> = 1,2,3,4. If a column is legal (TRY),
* mark the three "used" slots and advance to row R+1. If we run past
* row 4 we have a full solution -- PRINT Q<1..4> and BACK up. If a
* column fails, NXT bumps to the next column. If every column at row R
* fails, BACK up to row R-1, unmark its slots, and try its next column.
* The search ends when we back past row 1.
* Expected output (the only two 4-queens solutions, one column per row):
*   2 4 1 3
*   3 1 4 2
        Q = ARRAY('1:4')
        UC = ARRAY('1:4')
        D1 = ARRAY('1:8')
        D2 = ARRAY('1:7')
        R = 1
        Q<1> = 1
TRY     GT(R,4) :S(PRINT)
        T = Q<R>
        GT(T,4) :S(BACK)
        T = UC<T>
        EQ(T,1) :S(NXT)
        T = Q<R>
        D = R + T
        T = D1<D>
        EQ(T,1) :S(NXT)
        T = Q<R>
        D = R - T
        D = D + 4
        T = D2<D>
        EQ(T,1) :S(NXT)
        T = Q<R>
        UC<T> = 1
        T = Q<R>
        D = R + T
        D1<D> = 1
        T = Q<R>
        D = R - T
        D = D + 4
        D2<D> = 1
        R = R + 1
        Q<R> = 1
        :(TRY)
NXT     T = Q<R>
        T = T + 1
        Q<R> = T
        :(TRY)
PRINT   OUTPUT = Q<1>
        OUTPUT = Q<2>
        OUTPUT = Q<3>
        OUTPUT = Q<4>
BACK    R = R - 1
        EQ(R,0) :S(END)
        T = Q<R>
        UC<T> = 0
        T = Q<R>
        D = R + T
        D1<D> = 0
        T = Q<R>
        D = R - T
        D = D + 4
        D2<D> = 0
        T = Q<R>
        T = T + 1
        Q<R> = T
        :(TRY)
END
